WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.000
Hey! Squishy!

2
00:00:05.066 --> 00:00:08.366
Where are you, Squishy? Answer us!

3
00:00:13.433 --> 00:00:15.200
Squishy?

4
00:00:16.066 --> 00:00:18.833
Ash. Serena. Did you find it?

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.733
- No.
- Where could it have gone?

6
00:00:25.166 --> 00:00:26.466
Oh, Squishy.

7
00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:37.000
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

8
00:00:37.066 --> 00:00:41.033
♪ Knock me down, I'll just get up again ♪

9
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.233
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

10
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.133
♪ Pokémon ♪

11
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.600
- ♪ Pokémon ♪
- ♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

12
00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:51.866
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

13
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:53.866
♪ Pokémon ♪

14
00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:56.733
- ♪ Pokémon ♪
- ♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

15
00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:19.166
- Bonnie?
- Huh?

16
00:01:19.566 --> 00:01:20.833
You need to eat something.

17
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.433
You've gotta have your strength if you wanna find Squishy.

18
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.666
Pikachu.

19
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.200
Thanks, everybody.

20
00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:31.900
I wonder how Squishy is. I sure hope it's okay.

21
00:01:32.266 --> 00:01:34.366
I'm sure Squishy's doing just fine.

22
00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:36.633
I think you'll feel better if you eat something.

23
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:37.833
Clemont's right.

24
00:01:38.466 --> 00:01:39.400
Yeah.

25
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.733
- The Cells.
- So many.

26
00:01:49.066 --> 00:01:51.100
- Cells.
- What, Clemont?

27
00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:53.933
I remember what those people said.

28
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.133
They were talking about cells while they were after Squishy.

29
00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.333
There's no doubt Squishy possesses mysterious powers,

30
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.000
an unusual Pokémon.

31
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.166
No doubt about that.

32
00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.466
I know. That's why they're chasing it.

33
00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:13.233
I hate this! Maybe they're chasing Squishy right now.

34
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.600
Maybe they caught it and they're doing all sorts of bad stuff.

35
00:02:16.666 --> 00:02:19.233
We've gotta save Squishy. Squishy's in trouble!

36
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.233
- Bonnie, stop!
- Try to relax.

37
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.200
- Come on, Clemont. You're worried, too.
- Of course I'm worried.

38
00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:28.233
But it's too dangerous to go looking for Squishy this late.

39
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.966
It's dangerous for Squishy, too. Squishy!

40
00:02:32.433 --> 00:02:34.400
- Bonnie, wait!
- Hey, let go!

41
00:02:34.466 --> 00:02:37.000
You're supposed to listen to your big brother.

42
00:02:37.066 --> 00:02:40.500
- But what about Squishy, huh?!
- It's not just Squishy!

43
00:02:40.566 --> 00:02:42.100
What if something happens to you?

44
00:02:50.633 --> 00:02:51.633
Bonnie?

45
00:02:54.066 --> 00:02:57.233
I promised. I said I'd always protect it.

46
00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.600
I promised I'd make sure it was safe.

47
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:01.833
I know.

48
00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:05.033
We'll find Squishy tomorrow, I give my word.

49
00:03:07.866 --> 00:03:08.966
Mm-hm.

50
00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.733
All right. We need to sleep.

51
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.666
Let's all wash up and get ready.

52
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.233
Okay.

53
00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:34.933
She's asleep.

54
00:03:35.366 --> 00:03:37.200
Thank you so much, Serena.

55
00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:40.866
I totally understand why Bonnie's so worried.

56
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.300
Who are those people anyway?

57
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:45.900
And what are they gonna do if they catch Squishy?

58
00:03:46.566 --> 00:03:49.133
There are far more questions than answers.

59
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.133
You know, maybe Squishy really did run away from us.

60
00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.700
Well, even so, I'd like Bonnie to be able to say goodbye.

61
00:03:57.266 --> 00:04:00.333
We have to find Squishy, for Bonnie's sake.

62
00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.600
Not only that.

63
00:04:01.666 --> 00:04:05.200
We know it's Bonnie's friend, but Squishy's our friend, too.

64
00:04:05.866 --> 00:04:08.200
- Let's look first thing tomorrow.
- Right.

65
00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.433
This is the pursuit team reporting in.

66
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.166
The trainers in question have yet to make contact with Z1.

67
00:04:16.633 --> 00:04:19.533
- Continue to observe them.
- Roger.

68
00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.633
Tell me, what's the scanner showing?

69
00:04:22.166 --> 00:04:24.633
It's not showing a thing. Argh.

70
00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.200
It appears Z1's whereabouts are still unknown.

71
00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:30.533
Wow, that thing really likes to play hide-and-seek.

72
00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.300
Let's find it already.

73
00:04:32.366 --> 00:04:35.233
- Focus the scanner on a wider area.
- You got it.

74
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.366
Okay, time to get going, Bonnie.

75
00:04:41.433 --> 00:04:42.300
Pika, Pika.

76
00:04:42.366 --> 00:04:44.666
Dedenne, let's go.

77
00:04:45.466 --> 00:04:49.066
Just a second. I have a method for locating Squishy.

78
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.133
Yeah? What's that?

79
00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:57.000
Simple. Remember, the future is now, thanks to science.

80
00:04:57.066 --> 00:04:58.866
Clemontic Gear, on!

81
00:04:58.933 --> 00:05:01.633
It's the perfect device to search for Squishy.

82
00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.766
I call it the "Track Down Squishy for Certain, Mark One!"

83
00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:07.000
I'm counting on you, Clemont.

84
00:05:07.066 --> 00:05:09.033
Count on the power of science.

85
00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.033
My brilliantly designed machine will automatically search out

86
00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:15.333
and find the kinds of sunny places Squishy loves so much.

87
00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.866
Hold on. When did you find the time to make that?

88
00:05:18.333 --> 00:05:22.600
Making a useful machine for a dear sister is what being an inventor is all about.

89
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.566
Thank you.

90
00:05:25.933 --> 00:05:29.533
Now, "Track Down Squishy for Certain, Mark One," let's go.

91
00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.233
Show everyone just what you can do.

92
00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:35.800
- Huh?
- Did it find Squishy already?

93
00:05:35.866 --> 00:05:37.466
All right. Come on!

94
00:05:37.866 --> 00:05:38.700
Pika!

95
00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.000
Hmm!

96
00:05:41.066 --> 00:05:43.733
Who would've thought Squishy would have that much strength

97
00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:44.800
at its disposal?

98
00:05:44.866 --> 00:05:47.800
If we get our paws on that hot shot, conquering the world

99
00:05:47.866 --> 00:05:50.533
will be a piece of cake with ice cream on the side.

100
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.933
It's just the fancy glasses gang in our way.

101
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.300
They do look like the perfect picture of health.

102
00:05:56.366 --> 00:05:58.900
A little rest and relaxation and we'll be charged up

103
00:05:58.966 --> 00:06:01.733
and ready to rumble with those rowdy rascals.

104
00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.300
Wobbuffet!

105
00:06:09.666 --> 00:06:11.166
Hey, what's this?

106
00:06:15.966 --> 00:06:18.733
Ah! What's that?

107
00:06:20.866 --> 00:06:24.000
- Stop getting in our faces!
- You're keeping me from my beauty rest!

108
00:06:24.066 --> 00:06:26.166
I'm putting my foot down.

109
00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:36.400
That doesn't sound like a party to me.

110
00:06:36.466 --> 00:06:39.500
It's times like this that we should trust our instincts,

111
00:06:39.566 --> 00:06:41.000
and that's to run away.

112
00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:43.533
Wobbu, Wobbu!

113
00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.400
I don't get it. Where did your machine go?

114
00:06:51.066 --> 00:06:55.100
Don't worry. I installed a tracking device to see just where it goes.

115
00:07:00.166 --> 00:07:03.300
-Oh, no! My magnificent machine!

116
00:07:06.366 --> 00:07:07.466
Whoa, Toxicroak?

117
00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:10.966
Toxicroak,

118
00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:14.500
the Toxic Mouth Pokémon and the evolved form of Croagunk.

119
00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.966
Toxicroak's throat has a poison sac,

120
00:07:17.033 --> 00:07:20.966
and its poison stirs and becomes even more potent when it croaks.

121
00:07:21.533 --> 00:07:23.166
They look like they're mad.

122
00:07:23.666 --> 00:07:26.166
Maybe Clemont's invention did something bad to them.

123
00:07:26.233 --> 00:07:27.800
That's why it got beat up.

124
00:07:28.233 --> 00:07:31.033
- I think you're right.
- Toxicroak!

125
00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:33.100
Bunnelby, use Mud Shot.

126
00:07:39.066 --> 00:07:40.133
Now's our chance.

127
00:07:41.366 --> 00:07:43.266
Why can't we all be friends?

128
00:07:43.333 --> 00:07:44.633
Stop it, Toxicroak!

129
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.033
Aipom Arm, activate!

130
00:08:00.466 --> 00:08:01.800
Bonnie, no!

131
00:08:01.866 --> 00:08:03.266
Bunnelby, no!

132
00:08:13.566 --> 00:08:14.500
Bonnie.

133
00:08:15.033 --> 00:08:16.733
- Are you all right?
- Ah!

134
00:08:17.666 --> 00:08:19.800
I think I'm okay.

135
00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:21.433
Oh, thank goodness.

136
00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.966
Huh?

137
00:08:30.866 --> 00:08:33.000
- Bunnelby.
- Oh, no, what's wrong?

138
00:08:33.066 --> 00:08:34.366
Bunnelby.

139
00:08:36.433 --> 00:08:38.333
That's not good.

140
00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.533
- Hang in there, Bunnelby.

141
00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:42.566
It needs treatment now.

142
00:08:42.633 --> 00:08:44.833
We need to go to the Pokémon Center.

143
00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.100
You'll be fine. Just hang on. Hm!

144
00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:53.700
It appears the twerps haven't been able to reunite with Squishy as of yet.

145
00:08:53.766 --> 00:08:57.633
If we stay close to those yahoos, we'll find that cagey little critter.

146
00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:00.733
If not, we'll just take Pikachu. Simple.

147
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.500
My kind of operation.

148
00:09:02.566 --> 00:09:03.633
Wobbuffet!

149
00:09:08.866 --> 00:09:11.000
The scanner is picking up Z2's energy.

150
00:09:11.533 --> 00:09:14.600
Z1 appears to be responding, but it's out of range.

151
00:09:15.566 --> 00:09:20.866
I wonder. Are Z1 and Z2 having some kind of secret conversation or something?

152
00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.033
Fine-tune the scanner.

153
00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.600
- Determine Z1's location.
- You got it.

154
00:09:31.766 --> 00:09:35.300
Danger. Extreme. Exercise caution.

155
00:09:35.766 --> 00:09:38.866
Humans. Contact them no more.

156
00:09:40.766 --> 00:09:42.300
Not necessarily.

157
00:09:42.366 --> 00:09:46.466
I want to observe what humans are truly like.

158
00:09:46.866 --> 00:09:49.233
Do not support humans.

159
00:09:49.466 --> 00:09:52.266
Humans destroy order.

160
00:09:52.333 --> 00:09:54.000
They are destructive.

161
00:09:54.066 --> 00:09:57.800
The collapse of Kalos... is in progress.

162
00:09:58.233 --> 00:10:00.833
I do not share your views.

163
00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.266
I will not honor your request.

164
00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.233
Who's that Pokémon?

165
00:10:25.566 --> 00:10:27.533
It's Toxicroak.

166
00:10:28.133 --> 00:10:29.633
Toxic!

167
00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.900
Nurse Joy, will Bunnelby get better?

168
00:10:37.166 --> 00:10:39.133
Of course. It's just...

169
00:10:40.166 --> 00:10:41.566
I'm out of Nicera.

170
00:10:43.166 --> 00:10:44.200
Nicera?

171
00:10:44.866 --> 00:10:46.666
-Huh?

172
00:10:46.733 --> 00:10:47.800
Is this it?

173
00:10:48.733 --> 00:10:50.566
Yes. It's a medicinal plant.

174
00:10:50.633 --> 00:10:53.433
It grows on the mountaintop nearby, so I'll run and get some.

175
00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:56.233
Excuse me. Excuse me, Nurse Joy!

176
00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.700
- Please come look.
- Yes, right away.

177
00:10:58.766 --> 00:11:01.000
Please, wait here one moment.

178
00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.233
Ah...

179
00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.200
We're too late.

180
00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.033
Tell me Z1's current location.

181
00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.933
It appears they're no longer transmitting signals, so I lost them.

182
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.600
You're so useless.

183
00:11:27.733 --> 00:11:29.600
This is Bryony. Do you read?

184
00:11:30.233 --> 00:11:32.533
Affirmative. This is the pursuit team.

185
00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.000
What's up with those trainers?

186
00:11:34.066 --> 00:11:37.466
Well, we've tracked their location to the Pokémon Center.

187
00:11:37.533 --> 00:11:39.500
One of their Pokémon has been injured,

188
00:11:39.566 --> 00:11:42.233
and they're forced to deal with that matter at the present time.

189
00:11:42.766 --> 00:11:43.900
Understood.

190
00:11:43.966 --> 00:11:46.933
It sounds to me like Z1 isn't their current priority.

191
00:11:47.633 --> 00:11:51.700
It's possible they simply gave up on it because they know we're after Z1.

192
00:11:51.766 --> 00:11:54.233
I guess that means they won't be coming back.

193
00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:58.333
All right, pursuit team, pull back.

194
00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:01.633
I think we're gonna focus our search on Area R.

195
00:12:06.433 --> 00:12:07.700
Huh?

196
00:12:07.766 --> 00:12:08.766
Where's Bonnie?

197
00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.633
Huh? She was here a minute ago.

198
00:12:12.033 --> 00:12:12.966
Huh?

199
00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:17.833
Could she...?

200
00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.333
Must save Bunnelby. I've got to.

201
00:12:26.866 --> 00:12:27.833
Bunnelby.

202
00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:31.233
It got hurt because I was being so selfish.

203
00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.800
I'm sure of it. Bunnelby!

204
00:12:39.366 --> 00:12:41.566
Yeah. Gotta be careful.

205
00:12:51.533 --> 00:12:53.133
I'm glad that's over with.

206
00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.533
-Huh?

207
00:12:58.566 --> 00:13:01.266
Okay. Let's go.

208
00:13:11.666 --> 00:13:12.833
Please let us through.

209
00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:15.900
We've gotta get to the mountaintop right away!

210
00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:37.833
Everyone.

211
00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:40.433
- Are you all right?
- I'm okay.

212
00:13:49.033 --> 00:13:51.200
Pikachu, Braixen, good job.

213
00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:53.000
- Pika!
- Braixen.

214
00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.833
Why did you go alone?

215
00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.400
Do you know how worried we were?

216
00:13:56.866 --> 00:13:58.566
It's totally my fault.

217
00:13:58.633 --> 00:14:01.833
Bunnelby got hurt really badly because of me.

218
00:14:02.233 --> 00:14:04.833
Huh? Because of you?

219
00:14:07.266 --> 00:14:10.733
You're wrong. Bunnelby saw how desperate you were to find Squishy

220
00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.066
and wanted to help you.

221
00:14:12.133 --> 00:14:13.533
Help me? But I...

222
00:14:14.366 --> 00:14:18.866
Don't you get it? Squishy's just as precious to us as he is to you.

223
00:14:18.933 --> 00:14:19.766
Mm?

224
00:14:20.233 --> 00:14:23.033
Yes, of course. Squishy's our friend, too.

225
00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:25.266
All of us wanna make certain it's safe.

226
00:14:27.033 --> 00:14:28.300
Oh, Clemont.

227
00:14:28.833 --> 00:14:31.600
You should listen to your brother. He's right.

228
00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.600
- Pikachu!
- Braixen.

229
00:14:34.566 --> 00:14:36.133
You guys...

230
00:14:37.433 --> 00:14:39.900
First thing we've gotta do is find that plant.

231
00:14:39.966 --> 00:14:42.733
The sooner we do that, the sooner Bunnelby gets well.

232
00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:44.633
- Yeah.
- Right.

233
00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:45.900
Let's go now.

234
00:14:45.966 --> 00:14:47.100
- Pika!
- Braixen.

235
00:14:48.566 --> 00:14:50.333
-Pikachu, no!

236
00:14:52.833 --> 00:14:55.200
Prepare for trouble, the name is correct.

237
00:14:55.266 --> 00:14:57.566
But you saying no has little effect.

238
00:14:57.633 --> 00:14:59.800
To protect the world from devastation.

239
00:14:59.866 --> 00:15:02.700
To unite all people within our nation.

240
00:15:02.766 --> 00:15:05.666
We may want Squishy, but Squishy's not here.

241
00:15:05.733 --> 00:15:08.366
But Pikachu's someone we always hold dear.

242
00:15:09.233 --> 00:15:10.933
- Jesse.
- And James.

243
00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.466
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light.

244
00:15:14.533 --> 00:15:17.400
We always succeed because we fight the good fight.

245
00:15:17.466 --> 00:15:18.866
Meowth, that's right!

246
00:15:18.933 --> 00:15:20.466
Wobbuffet!

247
00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:23.533
Team Rocket?

248
00:15:24.366 --> 00:15:26.666
In our book, Pikachu's always a prize.

249
00:15:26.733 --> 00:15:28.733
We keep our eyes on the ball.

250
00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:30.466
Success is the way we roll.

251
00:15:30.533 --> 00:15:33.500
- So, now we're rolling out.
- Wobbu!

252
00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.000
Pikachu!

253
00:15:35.066 --> 00:15:36.666
We'll take care of these guys.

254
00:15:36.733 --> 00:15:38.600
Okay, Clemont and Bonnie...

255
00:15:38.866 --> 00:15:40.833
You two go and get that plant.

256
00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:42.933
- And hurry!
- Yup, got it.

257
00:15:43.266 --> 00:15:45.100
- Let's do it.
- Mm-hm.

258
00:15:48.333 --> 00:15:50.733
- Greninja, come on out.
- Ninja!

259
00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.900
- Quick. Water Shuriken!
- Now, Braixen, Flamethrower!

260
00:16:00.733 --> 00:16:04.466
I'm sorry, but this is all happening too quickly for my taste.

261
00:16:05.933 --> 00:16:07.166
Pika!

262
00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:10.566
Pikachu! Ha-ha.

263
00:16:10.633 --> 00:16:12.566
- That didn't take long.
- Pika, Pika.

264
00:16:12.633 --> 00:16:14.566
Why you-- Gourgeist!

265
00:16:14.633 --> 00:16:16.166
You too, Inkay.

266
00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.166
Everybody ready?

267
00:16:22.233 --> 00:16:23.366
Ready!

268
00:16:27.266 --> 00:16:28.933
Looks like this is the summit.

269
00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.500
- The Nicera.
- I wonder where it could be.

270
00:16:31.566 --> 00:16:33.200
Huh? Over there.

271
00:16:34.033 --> 00:16:34.866
Look.

272
00:16:35.266 --> 00:16:36.466
Oh...

273
00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:44.166
We found it.

274
00:16:44.233 --> 00:16:47.266
- Bonnie, that's Nicera.
- Yay!

275
00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.400
Bunnelby will be better in no time.

276
00:16:50.466 --> 00:16:52.766
Yeah. Let's bring some back right away.

277
00:16:59.266 --> 00:17:00.833
Pika!

278
00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:03.200
Okay, Inkay, now use Psybeam.

279
00:17:03.266 --> 00:17:04.599
Now, Dark Pulse.

280
00:17:08.099 --> 00:17:09.666
Pikachu, use Iron Tail.

281
00:17:09.966 --> 00:17:11.500
Greninja, use Aerial Ace.

282
00:17:12.333 --> 00:17:14.166
Braixen, use Scratch.

283
00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:23.099
All right, Pikachu, Thunderbolt.

284
00:17:23.166 --> 00:17:24.566
Greninja, Water Shuriken.

285
00:17:24.633 --> 00:17:26.433
Braixen, Fire Blast!

286
00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:38.566
We're blasting off again!

287
00:17:38.633 --> 00:17:40.866
- Inkay!
- Wobbuffet!

288
00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.766
- We did it.
- Braixe.

289
00:17:43.833 --> 00:17:46.366
- Great job, all of you!
- Pika!

290
00:17:46.433 --> 00:17:49.400
Now, let's go catch up to Clemont and Bonnie.

291
00:17:49.466 --> 00:17:50.366
Right.

292
00:17:56.133 --> 00:17:58.200
Bunnelby will get better with this.

293
00:17:58.266 --> 00:17:59.866
Just a little bit more.

294
00:18:13.866 --> 00:18:15.433
Whoa. Whoa!

295
00:18:19.133 --> 00:18:20.733
Let's try it once more.

296
00:18:39.066 --> 00:18:41.066
-All right!

297
00:18:41.533 --> 00:18:43.800
Bonnie. Dedenne. Ah!

298
00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:48.266
Hey, thanks for the lift.

299
00:18:48.333 --> 00:18:49.533
You're most welcome.

300
00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:51.966
Clemont. Bonnie. Hey, you guys!

301
00:18:52.366 --> 00:18:55.033
We found it.

302
00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.466
Good job, Bonnie.

303
00:18:57.866 --> 00:19:00.833
- Now we can make Bunnelby better.
- You bet.

304
00:19:01.333 --> 00:19:04.500
Everything's gonna be fine.

305
00:19:13.866 --> 00:19:16.800
I'm happy to report that Bunnelby's feeling just fine.

306
00:19:18.133 --> 00:19:20.433
Bunnelby, I was worried about you.

307
00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:23.700
We're all back together and Bunnelby feels fine.

308
00:19:24.233 --> 00:19:26.700
- Thank you all so much.
- Bunnelby!

309
00:19:26.766 --> 00:19:28.000
Mm-mm.

310
00:19:28.066 --> 00:19:31.533
We all did this together. I'm thanking you right back.

311
00:19:33.366 --> 00:19:36.500
All right, you guys. Now that Bunnelby's doing okay,

312
00:19:36.566 --> 00:19:38.633
let's head on back and look for Squishy.

313
00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:40.366
- Right.
- Let's get going.

314
00:19:40.433 --> 00:19:41.433
Bunnelby!

315
00:19:46.366 --> 00:19:49.066
- Let's try somewhere sunny, okay?
- Squishy loves sunshine.

316
00:19:49.133 --> 00:19:51.466
- Dedenne, what's wrong?
- Yeah, let's go. Hurry!

317
00:20:00.966 --> 00:20:02.766
Ah! Squishy!

318
00:20:02.833 --> 00:20:04.300
What? No way.

319
00:20:04.366 --> 00:20:08.000
You have no idea how worried we've been about you.

320
00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:10.866
What do you know?

321
00:20:10.933 --> 00:20:14.600
There's no doubt Squishy's been looking for Bonnie all this time as well.

322
00:20:14.666 --> 00:20:16.000
I'm sure.

323
00:20:16.066 --> 00:20:18.800
Are you gonna travel with us again, Squishy?

324
00:20:18.866 --> 00:20:20.100
Please say you will.

325
00:20:23.166 --> 00:20:25.000
Thank you, Squishy!

326
00:20:25.066 --> 00:20:27.100
- Yay! Ha-ha-ha.
- That's great news, Bonnie.

327
00:20:27.166 --> 00:20:31.100
You're staying with me. I promise we're always gonna be together.

328
00:20:33.533 --> 00:20:35.533
Squishy is back with our heroes,

329
00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.533
moved by Bonnie's caring heart and affection.

330
00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:42.966
But what exactly is Squishy, and what is it after?

331
00:20:43.266 --> 00:20:47.700
There are more answers to come as the journey continues.
